According to the document below the device is a 16-bit parallel I/O
card hardware and software compatible with the DRV-11.

DT-2768    a general purpose 16-bit digital input/output interface.
           Software and hardware compatible to DEC DRV-11 option.

DT-2768-I  Identical to DT2768 except that all input/output lines
           are optically isolated.

http://www.bitsavers.org/pdf/dataTranslation/DTI-UM-SP101-3_Sep80.pdf
  page 8

(The Data Translation DT2781 is an analog-to-digital converter.
There's a bitsavers manual for that.)

A google search for "bitsavers drv11" turns up manual, schematic and
diagnostic resources. The diagnostic I saw is a papertape, but they're
pretty easy to convert. There may be others.










