have blanked themselves in what seems a rather short time.  For example:
before I bought my new EPROM Programmers I tried to use onw of my old
one's.  I have two, both connect to ISA boards.  I tried every machine
I had with an ISA slot in it.  These included a Gateway, a Tandy and a
few no-names we hand built at the University years ago.  All have sat
in my basement for at leat 10 years without being turned on.  None of
them would boot.  Not even POST.  No beep, nothing at all.  As an old
fachioned scrounge I bulled all the memory and EPROMs before dumping them.
All of the EPROMs were blank when tested in the Programmer, pretty much
as I expected.

May seem unreasonable, but that's reality.  I don't know if there is
some kind of refresh that occurs when they are used, but I have more
than enough evidence that if they sit idle it only takes a couple
years for an EPROM to fade.

