Any machine/OS can read it. The question might be if there is some 
standard tool to do it, or if you need to write a program for it.

In RSX, you always have TPC, which can deal with this. And in new 
versions, you also have VCP.

I don't know what tools might be around in RT-11 or RSTS/E, but writing 
your own program always works.

Afraid I can't help in general, as any PDP-11 with tape drive I could 
use is far enough from me that I only go there about twice a year.

By the way, it's important to tell what density this tape is in, as it 
might affect if people can help. There is also an off-chance that the 
reel diameter might be important (there were tape drives which couldn't 
take all sizes).

