jjh <jjhudak@gmail.com> wrote:

(snip)

> The tape density is 800 bpi and our  9 track drive was
> a cipher (can't remember the model number) with a vacuum column
> arrangement.

800 bpi tapes are not good for portability.  They are very 
sensitive to head azimuth.  That is, the exact alignment of the
head such that the bits come out at the same time.  (All tracks
clock together.)  1600 bpi PE clocks each track separately, such
that it is fairly insensitive to head alignment (azimuth).

> I've located a 9-track locally but it had not been used in a 
> while and when we tried it, we got read/write errors and 
> haven't tracked down the problem yet.

Could be the drive, or it could have been written on a drive
that was out of alignment, or both.

-- glen


