glen herrmannsfeldt <gah@ugcs.caltech.edu> writes:

> The story I remember from IBM drives is that after a few tries
> and failures reading a block it automatically does some kind of
> head cleaning operation and tries again.  

Not just IBM tape drives.  All of the drives of my acquaintance have this
(mis)feature.

Why is it a MISfeature?  Because it's not a *HEAD* cleaning action, it's a
*TAPE* cleaning action.  The assumption is that there is crap of some kind
on the oxide, so scrape it gently to remove the crap.

An if-y tape can be permanently damaged by this.

By the way, Happy DEC-10 Day, everyone!

